SLUG: privacy.html
TITLE: Privacy Policy | Akash Movers, Kanpur
DESC: What this website collects when you request a moving quote, why, who it is shared with, how long it is kept, and how to have it deleted.
HEADING: Privacy policy
LEAD: What this website collects, why, and how to get it removed. Written to describe what the site actually does rather than to cover every eventuality.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Privacy|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow flow">

        <div class="demo-banner">
          <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-alert"/></svg>
          <div>
            <strong>Template — have this reviewed before you publish it.</strong>
            The technical description below is accurate for this website as
            built. The legal framing is not a substitute for advice: the
            business name, the identity of the data controller, the grievance
            officer required under India's data protection rules, and any
            sector-specific obligations must be filled in and checked by
            someone qualified. Replace this notice once that is done.
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          We collect personal information in one place only: the callback
          form. Nothing on this site tracks you around the web, and there are
          no advertising cookies.
        </p>
        <p>The form asks for four things, two of them optional:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your name</li>
          <li>Your mobile number</li>
          <li>Where you are moving from, if you choose to tell us</li>
          <li>Where you are moving to, if you choose to tell us</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We also record that you ticked the consent box, the page you were on
          when you sent it, and the time it arrived.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is deliberately short. The form used to ask for an email
          address, a WhatsApp number, PIN codes, property type, move date,
          floor numbers, lift availability and free-text notes. It no longer
          does: everything beyond a name and a number is a question for the
          phone call, and information that is never collected cannot be lost,
          leaked or misused.
        </p>

        <h2>What we deliberately do not collect</h2>
        <p>
          We do not store your IP address with your enquiry. An IP address is
          used only in memory, as a one-way hash, to limit how many
          submissions can come from one connection in an hour; that hash
          expires within the hour and is never attached to your record.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not use analytics by default. If analytics is ever switched
          on, this page will be updated to name the provider before it goes
          live.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>
          To prepare and discuss your moving quote, and to carry out the move
          if you book one. That is the only purpose. We ask for your consent
          on the form before you submit it, and you can withdraw that consent
          at any time using the contact details below.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no marketing opt-in on the form, and no promotional list.
          The only consent we ask for is consent to contact you about the
          enquiry you sent.
        </p>

        <h2>Who it is shared with</h2>
        <p>
          Your enquiry is sent to our own team so somebody can respond to it.
          If you are booking a move, the crew assigned to it will see the
          details they need to do the job.
        </p>
        <p>
          The technical services that carry the enquiry on our behalf are
          Cloudflare, which hosts this website and processes the form, and the
          WhatsApp Business Platform, operated by Meta, which delivers the
          notification to our team. We do not sell your information, and we do
          not pass it to other moving companies, lead brokers or advertisers.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Enquiry records are kept for <strong data-retention-days>365</strong>
          days and then deleted. If you book a move, records relating to the
          job itself may be kept longer where we are required to retain them,
          for example for tax purposes.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>You can ask us to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Tell you what we hold about you</li>
          <li>Correct anything that is wrong</li>
          <li>Delete your enquiry entirely</li>
          <li>Stop contacting you</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Use the contact details on our <a href="/contact.html">contact page</a>.
          Quote the reference number from your enquiry confirmation if you
          have it, as it makes the record easy to find. We will action
          deletion requests promptly.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served only over HTTPS. The form is processed on the
          server, not in your browser, and the credentials used to deliver the
          notification are held as encrypted environment variables that are
          never sent to your device. We do not store your enquiry in your
          browser's local storage.
        </p>
        <p>
          No website can promise it is impossible to attack. What we can say
          is that this one holds the minimum information needed to quote your
          move, for a limited time, behind standard protections.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes materially, the date below will change with
          it. This version was last updated on
          <time data-updated-date>11 October 2026</time>.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
